00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.460
GANG CHEN: A brief recap
of the last lecture,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.560
what we talked about is the
wave nature, wave particle

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.640
duality starting from
Planck, Einstein, relations.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.670
Energy is related frequency.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.080
Momentum is really to the
wavelength of the particle.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.370
And that lays the foundation
for the wave particle duality.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:55.290
Although Einstein focused
his effort on the photons.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:00.960
And later on this was
extended to the, say,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.580
the material waves.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.740
And for material waves, we have
different ways to describe it.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.380
There are different approaches--

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.490
metrics approach, the
operator approach.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:21.570
But the one that I use here
is the Schrodinger equation

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:26.250
that says, describe this
wave function, which is

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.350
a function of time and space.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.730
And the wave function on the
left hand side, essentially

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.410
this is like your
kinetic energy.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.470
This is a potential energy.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.340
And the right hand side
is a time dependent term.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.720
And the solution, as we
will see in today's lecture

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.970
of this equation, will give
you a wave type of solution.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:57.610
And what's interesting is the
meaning of this wave function

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:03.160
was not clear at the time that
this equation was written down.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.130
So then it turns out
that the explanation,

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:11.440
correct explanation,
of the wave function,

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.580
wave function itself,
is a complex number.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.270
Doesn't have physical meaning.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.610
But the wave function
times complex conjugate

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.560
will give a real number.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.930
And this gives the probability
of finding this material wave

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.850
at certain time and location.

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:36.010
So this is the explanation
given by Bourne.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.050
And that created
a lot of trouble

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.400
because that means everything is
uncertain in the quantum world.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.460
There's a probability, so
there is an expectation value,

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.890
the mean value.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.860
And there is also
standard deviation.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.300
And that standard deviation
to the Heisenberg uncertainty

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.890
principle we come under
in the last lecture.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:04.150
And then we did a
little bit mass.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.870
We say OK, let's do a
separation of variable.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.800
Because this wave function, it's
a function of time and space,

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.490
as long as this U,
potential energy that

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.900
constrain this material wave.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.750
So the equation is,
if you look at this,

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.970
the first term is
a kinetic energy.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.940
The second term is
the potential energy.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.130
And what's different
for each problem

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.810
is really this potential energy.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.760
The constraints are different.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.930
So if U is not
dependent on time,

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.150
then we can do
separation variable

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.990
to separate the wave function
into a space part and the time

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:42.490
part.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.730
Time part was easy.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.200
You can use it to solve it.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.060
And it turns out that separation
of variable constant, E,

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.510
has a physical meaning.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:56.120
And that meaning is the
energy of the system.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.070
And with that, we substitute
into from this time

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.310
dependent equation we
can get the steady state

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.580
equation, where
the steady state is

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.480
space dependent part of the
wave function can be determined.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.495
And you see that
this is actually

00:04:13.495 --> 00:04:15.520
an eigenvalue equation.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.940
It's here, here, on
the right hand side 0.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:25.310
So what you actually use is not
only find the wave function,

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:29.990
but also find the eigenvalue,
of the energy of the system.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.870
So this will put a constraint
on the possible energy

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:35.530
of a system.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.290
That's where the energy
quantization word naturally

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.040
came up.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.200
So this is where we were
in the last lecture.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.920
And today we will
use this equation

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.320
and give a few simple solutions.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.875
So today what we're going--

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.290
first I will give
example solutions.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.950
And if you recall, in
the first two lectures,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.990
we talk about what's the
energy of a molecule.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:18.160
We have kinetic energy.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.830
We have vibrational
energy, rotational energy,

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.600
electronic energy.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.920
And I'm going to use the quantum
mechanical Schrodinger equation

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.500
to say what are the
Schrodinger equation quantum

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:35.240
mechanics imposed on this energy
forms and the quantization.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:42.040
And then from this we will
say some important concept.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.165
What is the quantum state?

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:53.129
And what are the degeneracy?

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:07.510
And if you'll recall that we
talked about the the counting.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.210
We say, OK, how many
particles we have.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:14.650
And this degeneracy
is an important step

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:18.520
in doing the correct
accounting when we later on do

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.840
the transport problem.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.840
So count how much energy
the system really has.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:28.990
So let's start with
the example solutions.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.250
And we said the difference
for each problem

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:50.790
is really that potential U. The
first part is a kinetic energy.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:54.000
Once you know the mass,
that's a term you have.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.930
And each problem, each
particle, is constrained

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.420
by different potentials.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.880
Our air molecule in this
room, electron in a film,

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.400
or the vibration
energy, those are

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.590
different potential constraints.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:14.100
So let's look at the
first, the simplest one.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:18.820
There's no potential, no
constraint of free particle--

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.980
complete free.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.080
And let's look at 1D.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.290
So we don't need to write
a three dimension, so

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.325
1D free particle.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.690
What does that tell you?

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:41.190
So we have, already,
the time dependent term.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.390
And so we only need to go to
find out from the steady state

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.340
the space dependent term.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:55.060
By combined together, we know
what's the wave function.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.700
And if it's free,
there's no constraint.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:03.500
This U, the potential
energy is 0 everywhere.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:09.400
And so my steady state equation,
if you copy that into 1D,

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:22.330
is minus h bar squared 2m, d
plus i, dx minus E plus psi

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.010
equals 0.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:28.410
E is the energy
of this particle,

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:32.220
the eigenvalue of the problem.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:37.559
And this equation I think
you can all solve it.

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:39.270
Let's go one more step.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:43.780
I put them together,
this constant.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:48.900
So what I have is k
squared plus psi equals 0.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:57.150
Well, this K squared is 2m
E divided by H bar squared.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:03.760
That's just a notation
for my [INAUDIBLE]..

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.650
And I solve this equation second
order, differentiable equation

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:13.660
with the constant coefficient
k, not a space dependent term.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.840
That's the easy one.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.350
So you find the
characteristic root

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.390
of this characteristic equation.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.400
That's a plus minus k.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:28.370
So what we have is the
psi x is a, E minus

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:35.860
ikx plus b e plus ikx.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.812
Do you agree?

00:09:36.812 --> 00:09:37.645
That's the solution.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:46.750
Now we combine this
space-dependent solution

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:52.390
with the time-dependent
solution minus iE h bar.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.570
So that's a time-dependent.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:01.360
And the E, I say it's the
energy, E equals h nu.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.280
So I could write this--

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:12.760
so the wave function as a
function of time and space

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:19.750
could be then written as an
exponential minus i omega t

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:30.310
plus kx plus b exponential
minus i omega t minus kx.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:35.230
Well, this E equals h bar omega.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:39.040
H bar is h over 2 pi.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:44.890
So this is angular
frequency rather than nu.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.540
Omega is 2 pi nu.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:55.000
So that's the solution for
this free particle in space,

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.190
from minus infinite
to plus infinite.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:11:01.420
What you can say is this
solution tells you--

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.680
the particle is a wave.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.360
This is a typical wave.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:10.050
This is a wave propagating
into which the direction?

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.180
Negative direction, x direction.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.850
Omega kt minus kx.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.950
Here is omega t plus kx.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.430
So you have two
counter-propagating waves

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.690
in free space.

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:25.720
And that's go from minus
infinite to plus infinite.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.760
The particle is everywhere.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:32.600
This is the uncertainty
for free particle.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.520
You can't pinpoint where it is.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:43.220
And so, that's
the free particle.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.720
And basically, it
tells us it's a wave.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:51.400
And if you look at this,
k is the wave vector.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:54.570
If you look at this wave,
k is the wave vector.

00:11:54.570 --> 00:12:00.710
And if I go to combine
and write a energy, what's

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:02.810
the energy of this particle?

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:08.840
Is h plus square k
square divided by 2m.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:13.830
Here, this is my definition
for k. k is a wave vector.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.000
I write the energy--

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:22.740
h bar k, go back to
the Einstein relation.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:27.105
Here, p equals h
lambda is h bar k.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.820
That's the momentum.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:37.700
So it comes back to
essentially the p square 2m,

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:43.370
that's the kinetic energy
free particle, kinetic energy,

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:50.030
momentum energy relation,
energy equals 1/2 mv squared.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:54.560
So this is the 1D free particle.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:58.070
And now let's put
a constraint on it.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:02.840
So 1D quantum well.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:14.760
And we already went to the web
and look at the people actually

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:15.970
working on quantum wells.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.440
So they deposit thin films.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.670
And in that case, the
electron in the film

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.350
is subject to the constraint.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:29.240
Because outside the film is
a vacuum or another material.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:34.400
So now, we give the
simplest potential form

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:39.150
for a say, constraint,
simple constraint.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.360
So here is the potential.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:46.640
Let's say, this is the film.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.940
If I deposit a solid film.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:57.050
And this is the thickness
0 to D. And potential,

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:02.860
let's say I take this
as 0, this as infinite.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.780
So that's a simplification.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.080
The real case, vacuum
may not be the difference

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.700
between a vacuum and the film.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.290
The energy is a pretty much the
work function of the electron,

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.120
we said before.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.810
That's a few electron volts.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.870
So it's not a 0 to infinite.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:24.700
But for simplicity
of my solution

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.100
here, I say here is
zero potential, here

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:28.652
is infinite potential.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:39.570
So what is the energy of the
electron or if it's a, say,

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:40.080
atom.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:45.600
Somehow I constrain the atom
between two parallel plates.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.450
What's the allowable energy?

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:53.700
If you recall two
lecture ago, we actually

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.280
gave a solution without
solving Schrodinger equation.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:59.550
We say you have standing waves.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:02.610
So we have a 1/2 wavelengths,
the full wavelengths.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.190
With that, we found
the energy before.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:09.210
And what are we're going to do
next is using the Schrodinger

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:16.380
equation and to derive the same
result. So here, energy is--

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.350
and here u is 0.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:25.260
So for the 0 part, let's
suppose I take my coordinate

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.690
x is going to be
between 0 and D.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:35.220
So between 0 and D, if you look
at the Schrodinger equation,

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:43.870
is essentially the same equation
because the potential is 0.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:49.030
And then, outside this region,
because potential is infinite,

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.580
so what's the wave
function value?

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:55.240
This is infinite.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:57.640
This has to be 0.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:00.340
So my boundary condition,
essentially at these two

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:03.400
points, wave function is 0.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.960
And in between, my
solution is here.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.750
So I'm going to use
this boundary condition,

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:11.785
use the solution.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:17.200
So we have-- the
solution is here.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.360
I'm going to not
repeat that solution.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:23.950
And in this case,
we have x equals 0.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:27.130
Wave function should be 0.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:33.590
And that tells me here when x
equals 0, this is 0, this is 1,

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.280
this is 1, a plus b equals 1.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:41.155
So I have a plus b equals 1.

00:16:41.155 --> 00:16:41.905
That's the first--

00:16:41.905 --> 00:16:44.632
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

00:16:44.632 --> 00:16:45.340
GANG CHEN: Oh, 0.

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.300
Sorry.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:47.600
a plus b equals 0.

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:48.100
Thank you.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.380
Yep.

00:16:53.380 --> 00:17:01.390
And x equal to D wave
function is 0 again.

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:15.800
So I have a exponential
minus ikx plus d, ikD, plus b

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:23.849
exponential plus ikD equals 0.

00:17:23.849 --> 00:17:25.680
So a equals minus b.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:29.100
So if a equals minus b,
I substitute in this.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.560
What I have?

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:32.790
I take that out.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:45.835
I will have a negative
2 ai sine kD equals 0.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:53.500
After I substitute the
first a equals minus b,

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.580
that's what I have.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:03.240
So I cannot have a equals
to 0, b equals to 0.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:08.680
If I have that, my wave function
is 0, I have nothing there.

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:17.200
So my only way to have this
meaningful is sine kD equals 0.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:22.780
And that means k times
D now has to be integer.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:31.750
Say, sine kD equals 0, those
are pi, 2 pi, every pi.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:39.880
So now I have to put a subscript
n, because this is n times pi.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:45.220
And the n could be 0 plus
or minus 1, plus or minus 2.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.440
So those are the
mathematical solutions.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:19:01.400
And this mathematical solution
tells me, kn now is quantized.

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:12.830
Kn is n pi over D. And that
kn is 2m En h bar square.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:19.310
So 2m En h bar square.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.770
So my energy becomes discreet.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:29.590
So from here, I
solve for the energy

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:32.605
of this particular equals--

00:19:32.605 --> 00:19:34.060
AUDIENCE: Square root.

